        "title": "Choose between options and get probabilities",
        "steps": [
          "In Python, create a `DecisionEngine` from `jevalt.engine` with a backend and model name.",
          "Call `predict` with a `state` text and a `questions` entry of type `choice`, with `instructions` and `criteria` for each option.",
          "Read `choice` and `probabilities` under `answers` in the result."
        ]
      },
      {
        "feature": "return calibrated probabilities for question types",
        "title": "Get calibrated probabilities for each question type",
        "steps": [
          "In the `questions` passed to `predict`, set `type` to `choice`, `score` or `noul`.",
          "For `score`, give `criteria` as a list of levels. For `noul`, give a single criterion.",
          "Read the `probabilities`, `score` or `noul` value for each question under `answers`."
        ]
      },
      {
        "feature": "return unknown option with reasoning traces",
        "title": "Get an unknown option with reasoning traces",
        "steps": [
          "Add `\"abstain\": True` and `\"reasoning\": \"on\"` to the request passed to `predict`.",
          "Read `unknown` and `reasoning` for each question under `answers` in the result."
        ]
      }
    ]
